# Retained reads, publications, subscriptions, loss and overload over MQTT

## Goal

Consume an MQTT Thing through the runtime with the Lab's EMQTT client: read
a retained Property, publish a Property write and an Action invocation,
observe a Property through a linked broker session, and see what a missing
retained message, an unreachable broker, an oversized delivery and a lost
connection look like. The credential, when one is used, builds the CONNECT
packet only and is never kept.

## Prerequisites

```elixir
Mix.install([
  {:wotex_lab, "~> 0.1.0"},
  {:emqtt, "~> 1.15", system_env: [{"BUILD_WITHOUT_QUIC", "1"}]}
])
```

The requirements above are published-artifact requirements. At the time this
notebook was written none of the `wotex*` packages is published on Hex; the
notebook is verified against the workspace source cohort recorded in
`priv/provenance/source-cohort.json` by `test/wotex/lab/cookbook_test.exs`,
which evaluates every Elixir cell below in order (skipping this install
cell). `Mix.install/1` never points at a Git checkout. `emqtt` is an optional
dependency the host selects; it is compiled without its QUIC transport.

The notebook needs a peer. Inside the Lab checkout, the scripted in-BEAM
MQTT 5 peer from `test/support/mqtt_server.ex` is available and is used
automatically: it answers CONNECT, SUBSCRIBE, PUBLISH and PINGREQ, and lets a
cell inject a server DISCONNECT. It is a scripted test peer, not a broker.
Outside the checkout, bind `broker_href` (the automated `:broker` test does
this with a disposable `eclipse-mosquitto:2` container) or set
`WOTEX_LAB_MQTT_HREF`, for example after
`docker run --rm -p 1883:1883 eclipse-mosquitto:2`. Against a real broker the
fault-injection cells report `:not_simulated` and the checks they feed are
omitted, because a real broker cannot be told to drop the connection.

## Package and consumer ownership

| Concern | Owner | Where |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Form to topic/filter mapping, commands, delivery values, retained semantics | `wotex_binding_mqtt` (package-implements) | `Wotex.Binding.MQTT`, `Command`, `Delivery` |
| Subscription envelope, `:transport_down`, identity | `wotex_runtime` (package-implements) | `Wotex.Runtime.Subscription` |
| Connections, keep-alive, payload bounds, no automatic reconnect | `wotex_lab` (consumer-implements `Wotex.Binding.MQTT.Client`) | `Adapters.MQTT.EmqttClient`, `Adapters.MQTT.Session` |
| Reconnect | host decision through the subscription restart policy | `restart:` on the child spec |
| The peer | scripted test peer or a broker you run | see prerequisites |

## Run

```elixir
alias Wotex.Binding.MQTT
alias Wotex.Binding.MQTT.{Broker, Command, Transport, TransportConfig}
alias Wotex.Lab
alias Wotex.Lab.Adapters.MQTT.EmqttClient
alias Wotex.Lab.Adapters.Runtime.NoSec
alias Wotex.Lab.Error, as: LabError
alias Wotex.Lab.Telemetry
alias Wotex.Runtime.{ConsumedThing, Context, Error, ExecutionContext, Result}
alias Wotex.ThingDescription

telemetry_id = "cookbook-consume-mqtt-#{System.unique_integer([:positive])}"

events =
  for component <- Telemetry.components(),
      operation <- Telemetry.operations(),
      event <- [:start, :stop, :exception],
      do: [:wotex, :lab, component, operation, event]

:ok = :telemetry.attach_many(telemetry_id, events, &Telemetry.forward/4, self())
```

Select the peer: an explicit `broker_href` wins over the scripted peer.
Every run uses its own topic prefix so nothing retained by an earlier run is
read back.

```elixir
broker_href = Keyword.get(binding(), :broker_href) || System.get_env("WOTEX_LAB_MQTT_HREF")
scripted? = Code.ensure_loaded?(Wotex.Lab.Test.MqttServer) and broker_href == nil
prefix = "lab/cookbook/#{System.unique_integer([:positive])}"
temperature_topic = "#{prefix}/properties/temperature"
execution_context = ExecutionContext.new(Context.new!(request_id: "mqtt-direct"), nil)

peer =
  if scripted? do
    Wotex.Lab.Test.MqttServer.start(self(), retained: {temperature_topic, "21.5"}, on_exit: false)
  else
    nil
  end

interaction_href = if scripted?, do: Wotex.Lab.Test.MqttServer.href(peer), else: broker_href

if not scripted? do
  {:ok, broker} = Broker.new(interaction_href)
  {:ok, seed} = Command.publish(broker, :writeproperty, temperature_topic, 21.5, qos: 1, retain: true)
  :ok = EmqttClient.publish(seed, execution_context, %{connect_timeout: 2_000})
end

{scripted?, prefix}
```

The fixture TD names a placeholder broker and topic prefix; both are
rewritten before parsing. The transport configuration bounds deliveries to
eight bytes so an oversized message is observable later.

```elixir
fixture = Application.app_dir(:wotex_lab, "priv/fixtures/mqtt/thing-description.json")

{:ok, td} =
  fixture
  |> File.read!()
  |> String.replace("mqtt://127.0.0.1:1883", interaction_href)
  |> String.replace("lab/cookbook/room", prefix)
  |> ThingDescription.parse()

{:ok, mqtt_config} =
  TransportConfig.new(EmqttClient, %{connect_timeout: 2_000},
    read_timeout: 2_000,
    max_payload_bytes: 8
  )

{:ok, consumed} =
  ConsumedThing.new(td,
    profiles: [MQTT.profile()],
    transports: %{mqtt: {Transport, mqtt_config}},
    credentials: {NoSec, []}
  )

context = Context.new!(request_id: "mqtt-cookbook")
```

Retained read: the client subscribes, lets a PINGREQ round trip flush the
retained delivery, and tears the connection down. The result says the
delivery was retained.

```elixir
{:ok, %Result{} = retained} = ConsumedThing.read_property(consumed, "temperature", context)

connect_report =
  if scripted? do
    receive do
      {:mqtt_connect, %{username: username, password: password}} -> {username, password}
    after
      2_000 -> :no_connect_report
    end
  else
    :not_simulated
  end

{retained.payload, retained.metadata.delivery_retained, connect_report}
```

Publications: a Property write and an Action invocation each publish one
Application Message on the Form's topic and are `:accepted`.

```elixir
{:ok, %Result{status: write_status}} = ConsumedThing.write_property(consumed, "target", 23.5, context)
{:ok, %Result{status: action_status}} = ConsumedThing.invoke_action(consumed, "setTarget", 24, context)

published =
  if scripted? do
    receive_publish = fn receive_publish, acc ->
      receive do
        {:mqtt_publish, message} -> receive_publish.(receive_publish, [message | acc])
      after
        500 -> Enum.reverse(acc)
      end
    end

    receive_publish.(receive_publish, [])
  else
    :not_simulated
  end

{write_status, action_status, published}
```

Subscription: a linked session under the instance's `:sessions` role. The
retained message arrives first (`retained: true`), then a fresh publication.
The earlier bounded connections also reported their packets to this process;
those stale reports are flushed so the cell waits for this subscription's own
SUBSCRIBE.

```elixir
flush = fn flush ->
  receive do
    {:mqtt_subscribe, _filters} -> flush.(flush)
    :mqtt_pingreq -> flush.(flush)
    :mqtt_disconnect -> flush.(flush)
  after
    0 -> :ok
  end
end

:ok = flush.(flush)
{:ok, lab} = Lab.start_link(id: "consume-mqtt", max_children: 4)

{:ok, spec} =
  ConsumedThing.observation_child_spec(consumed, "temperature", context,
    id: :observe,
    receiver: self(),
    restart: :temporary
  )

{:ok, subscription} = Lab.start_child(lab, :sessions, spec)
monitor = Process.monitor(subscription)

if scripted? do
  receive do
    {:mqtt_subscribe, _filters} -> :ok
  after
    2_000 -> :no_subscribe
  end
end

retained_delivery =
  receive do
    {:wotex_runtime, :observe, {:ok, value, %{retained: true}}} -> value
  after
    5_000 -> :no_retained_delivery
  end

if scripted? do
  Wotex.Lab.Test.MqttServer.publish(peer, temperature_topic, "21.5")
else
  {:ok, broker} = Broker.new(interaction_href)
  {:ok, fresh} = Command.publish(broker, :writeproperty, temperature_topic, 21.5, qos: 1)
  :ok = EmqttClient.publish(fresh, execution_context, %{connect_timeout: 2_000})
end

delivery =
  receive do
    {:wotex_runtime, :observe, {:ok, value, %{retained: false} = meta}} -> {value, meta.topic}
  after
    5_000 -> :no_delivery
  end

{retained_delivery, delivery}
```

## Deliberate breakage

A Topic Filter without a retained message is a typed protocol error; an
unreachable broker is `:mqtt_connect_refused`; a delivery over the payload
bound is dropped, not forwarded; a server DISCONNECT ends the session with
`:transport_down`.

```elixir
{:ok, broker} = Broker.new(interaction_href)
empty_peer = if scripted?, do: Wotex.Lab.Test.MqttServer.start(self(), on_exit: false), else: nil
empty_href = if scripted?, do: Wotex.Lab.Test.MqttServer.href(empty_peer), else: interaction_href
{:ok, empty_broker} = Broker.new(empty_href)

{:ok, read_power} =
  Command.subscribe(empty_broker, :readproperty, "#{prefix}/properties/power", qos: 1, retain: true)

{:error, %LabError{code: no_retained}} =
  EmqttClient.read(read_power, 2_000, execution_context, %{connect_timeout: 2_000})

{:ok, closed_broker} = Broker.new("mqtt://127.0.0.1:1")
{:ok, unreachable_publish} = Command.publish(closed_broker, :writeproperty, "#{prefix}/x", 1, qos: 1)

{:error, %LabError{code: unreachable, class: unreachable_class}} =
  EmqttClient.publish(unreachable_publish, execution_context, %{connect_timeout: 1_000})

oversized =
  if scripted? do
    Wotex.Lab.Test.MqttServer.publish(peer, temperature_topic, "123456789012345")

    receive do
      {:wotex_runtime, :observe, message} -> {:delivered, message}
    after
      300 -> :dropped
    end
  else
    :not_simulated
  end

down =
  if scripted? do
    Wotex.Lab.Test.MqttServer.disconnect(peer)

    receive do
      {:wotex_runtime, :observe, {:status, status}} -> status
    after
      2_000 -> :no_status
    end
  else
    :not_simulated
  end

{no_retained, {unreachable, unreachable_class}, oversized, down}
```

```elixir
if scripted? do
  receive do
    {:DOWN, ^monitor, :process, ^subscription, _reason} -> :ok
  after
    2_000 -> :still_alive
  end
end

:ok = Supervisor.stop(lab)
if scripted?, do: Wotex.Lab.Test.MqttServer.stop(peer)
if scripted?, do: Wotex.Lab.Test.MqttServer.stop(empty_peer)
:ok
```

## Safe telemetry

Runtime spans name the operation and outcome; broker addresses, topics and
payloads are not labels.

```elixir
drain = fn drain ->
  receive do
    {:wotex_lab_telemetry, event, measurements, metadata} ->
      [{event, measurements, metadata} | drain.(drain)]
  after
    0 -> []
  end
end

spans = drain.(drain)
:telemetry.detach(telemetry_id)
text = inspect(spans)
labels_safe? = not (text =~ prefix) and not (text =~ "127.0.0.1") and not (text =~ "23.5")
{length(spans), labels_safe?}
```

## Expected output

| Check | Expectation |
| --- | --- |
| `retained-read` | The retained `21.5` is read with `delivery_retained: true` |
| `write-published` | The write is `:accepted` (and the peer saw the target topic when scripted) |
| `action-published` | The invocation is `:accepted` (and the peer saw the action topic when scripted) |
| `delivery-decoded` | A fresh publication reaches the receiver as `21.5` on the temperature topic |
| `unreachable-refused` | `mqtt://127.0.0.1:1` is `:mqtt_connect_refused`, class `:unavailable` |
| `no-retained-message` | An empty filter is `:no_retained_message` |
| `connect-reported` (scripted only) | The CONNECT carried no username or password |
| `oversized-dropped` (scripted only) | A 15-byte delivery over an 8-byte bound is dropped |
| `transport-down` (scripted only) | A server DISCONNECT is reported as `:transport_down` |

```elixir
base = %{
  "retained-read" => retained.payload == 21.5 and retained.metadata.delivery_retained,
  "write-published" =>
    write_status == :accepted and
      (not scripted? or Enum.any?(published, &(&1.topic == "#{prefix}/properties/target"))),
  "action-published" =>
    action_status == :accepted and
      (not scripted? or Enum.any?(published, &(&1.topic == "#{prefix}/actions/set-target"))),
  "delivery-decoded" => delivery == {21.5, temperature_topic},
  "unreachable-refused" => unreachable == :mqtt_connect_refused and unreachable_class == :unavailable,
  "no-retained-message" => no_retained == :no_retained_message and labels_safe?
}

faults = %{
  "connect-reported" => connect_report == {nil, nil},
  "oversized-dropped" => oversized == :dropped,
  "transport-down" => down == :transport_down
}

if scripted?, do: Map.merge(base, faults), else: base
```

## Public seam

`mqtt.client` — `Wotex.Binding.MQTT.Client.publish/3`, `read/4`,
`subscribe/4`, `unsubscribe/4` (consumer-implements; `EmqttClient`).
`runtime.credentials` (`NoSec` here; `StaticRef` supplies
`{:password, user, password}` for a `basic` scheme).

## Spec and completion IDs

* Lab: WLB.04 (`WLB-C04`, `WLB-C08`).
* Upstream consumer evidence: `WBM-C01`, `WBM-C02`, `WBM-C03`, `WBM-C04`.

## Replacement adapter

Implement `Wotex.Binding.MQTT.Client` with another MQTT library: `read/4`
must distinguish a missing retained message from a timeout, `subscribe/4`
must link a session to the owner and send `{:wotex_transport_frame,
%Wotex.Binding.MQTT.Delivery{}}` and `{:wotex_transport_status,
:transport_down}`, deliveries over the command's payload bound must be
dropped, and the client must not reconnect on its own or keep the credential
after CONNECT. Pass it as the module in `Wotex.Binding.MQTT.TransportConfig.new/3`.
